==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ganglion the Ancient''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ganglion the Unleashed''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Ganglion is like [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]]. Good enough stats, a good set of abilities, and a lot of speed. Unlike The Peach Devils, however, Ganglion's delay between attacks is entirely composed of a long backswing. This means that he will not move while recharging an attack, reducing the amount of potential damage he might absorb, and he'll be able to retaliate immediately after being knocked back. His lack of immunity to warp and knockback effects also helps to reset his long backswing and deal even more damage.

Ganglion serves well as a Long Distance rusher, able to cripple the backlines of enemies that would otherwise be a pain to deal with when the boss gets knocked back. He acts a good counter to [[Alpacky]] and [[Zamelle]] due to his high bulk as a rusher, as well as backliners with the knockback ability such as [[Mr. Mole]]. Like many units with high speed, Ganglion is also a viable counter to many [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemies]] such as [[Henry]], as he'll rush into their blind spots with hardly any timing required, and then do heavy damage from there.

Take note that unlike conventional rushers with very short attack animations, Ganglion has a 3-second foreswing which makes him very vulnerable to being juggled and may cause him to miss. Meatshielding is required to deal with melee enemies. The most obvious choice is [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]], as its Alien Resistance and high health can prevent melee Aliens from entering Ganglion's blind spot. He also has a long recharge time, so he can be difficult to replace when lost, somewhat contradicting his role.

==='''True Form'''===
Ganglion's True Form greatly increases his health and knockback count, simply making him even better at what he's already good at. Ganglion, even with his anti-Alien role, has a problem with [[Ursamajor]] and [[Cadaver Bear]] ([[Teacher Bear]] variants in general), where Ganglion's hits are disrupted by Cadaver's burrow or high DPS from Ursamajor's strengthen.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Weaken''' is Ganglion's first Talent, and it isn't particularly useful. It has a 50% chance, and lasts for up to 4 seconds at max, but with Ganglion's high damage, he's likely to just kill any enemies he hits instead of weakening them. On top of that, weaken isn't exactly the most useful status effect. '''Weaken Immunity''' shares a similar story, it might be useful against [[Calamary]] or a [[Zroco]] that burrows into him, but outside of that, this Talent likely won't help much. Like most Resist Talents, '''Resist Slow''' is very rarely worth even considering. '''Attack''' and '''HP Buff''' are helpful as always, though it's recommended to level Ganglion up using [[Catseye]]s before investing in these.

==='''Orb'''===
Strong Against Up against either Aliens or Zombies is recommended, as the HP boost would let Ganglion hit more enemies and the attack boost is always helpful.

