==Trivia==
*[[Ensanglion the Calamity]]'s description heavily implies that Ganglion is his virtuous twin, alter-ego, offshoot or clone and the one who sealed him away.
**The "Gan" in Ganglion's name can be taken as 贋 (counterfeit, fake), contrasting Ensanglion's Japanese name (シングリオン ''Shingurion'', "Shinglion" or "Singlion"), which may be derived from 真 ''shin'' (true).
**The term used for "bury" in Ganglion the Unleashed's Japanese description, 葬り去る ''hōmurisaru'', specifically refers to burying something like the past, not in the ground; leaving something to be forgotten. This may explain why Ganglion is regarded as the founder of all [[Lords of Destruction DRAGON EMPERORS (Gacha Event)|DRAGON EMPERORS]] rather than Ensanglion.
**The Japanese descriptions of Ganglion and [[Ultima Beast Naala]], another powerful, ancient [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], both use the word 始祖 ''shiso'' (founder or originator; the first person to start something, or the first in a lineage). Ganglion is said to be the founder/originator of all dragons (全てのドラゴンの始祖 ''subete no doragon no shiso''), while Naala is revered as the founder/originator of all beasts (全ての獣の始祖 ''subete no kemono no shiso'').
**The pink glow that Ensanglion's eyes get when attacking contrasts the [[Media:Ganglion promo.jpeg|green glow]] briefly seen in Ganglion's eyes during his attack animation.
**The most likely reason why Ganglion has an enemy counterpart as the final boss of [[Behemoth Culling]] is that he's an [[wikia:monsterhunter:Elder Dragon|Elder Dragon]], just like most of the "final bosses" of the ''Monster Hunter'' games, which nearly all of the Behemoths are references to.
**Ganglion the Unleashed's Weaken [[Talents|Talent]] is a possible reference to Ensanglion's ability to Weaken cats.
*Since several of the other Dragon Emperors appear to have been named after video games, Ganglion's name may be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Gungriffon|Gungriffon]]'', which is spelled and pronounced almost the same in Japanese:
**ガングリフォン ''Gangurifon'' (''Gungriffon'') → ガングリオン ''Gangurion'' (Ganglion)
*He is the third [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] to have an enemy counterpart, the others being [[Nuclear Dragon King Berius (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Nuclear Dragon King Berius]] and [[Princess Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Cat]].
*If one looks closely, they will notice that what appears to be Ganglion's tail is actually a back extension to his head/neck.
*The [[wikipedia:Star of David|Star of David]] appears in Ganglion the Ancient's attack animation, being the power-up circle seen directly before his attack. Ensanglion the Calamity has it behind him at almost all times.
*He is one of the three Dragon Emperors whose Cat face doesn't change to resemble a [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] in Evolved Form, the others being [[High Lord Babel (Legend Rare Cat)|High Lord Babel]] and [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|Sea King Daliasan]], whose Cat face resembles a [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]] instead.
*He is the only Dragon Emperor whose [[True Form]]'s name doesn't start with "God-Emperor".
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, though unlockable, the banner from which he originates from did not list him as an unlockable character, making it inaccurate. This was later fixed in Version 1.0.5.

